Vendored algorithm files (Kizuki TypeScript adaptations of the public tip):

- recipe/rrf.ts       from src/core/search/hybrid.ts
                      (RRF_K = 60, normalize, authority boost, 0.7/0.3 cosine blend)
- recipe/dedup.ts     from src/core/search/dedup.ts
                      (four-layer near-duplicate post-filter)
- recipe/degrade.ts   from src/core/search/hybrid.ts
                      (declared-degradation envelope)
- recipe/tier.ts      Kizuki mapping that replaces path-derived source boosts
- recipe/graph.ts     from src/core/search/graph-signals.ts and
                      src/core/search/two-pass.ts (adjacency + hop walk)
- recipe/types.ts     Kizuki port document/hit shapes
- recipe/index.ts     package surface

Modifications marked relative to the public tip:

- Product identifiers rewritten so they do not appear in this tree.
- SearchResult / BrainEngine types replaced by kizuki.retrieval/v1 shapes.
- Path-derived source-boost maps and personal slug prefixes were not copied.
- Authority is an orthogonal ranking axis: owner_correction outranks
  owner_authored, connector_evidence, then model_inference.
- Sensitivity is enforced by the port; unlabeled documents are never served.
- No environment-variable ranking overrides.
- No telemetry, query cache, or network client.
- No reranker and no local GGUF runtime (those remain Kizuki-own work).
- Graph signals fail closed on unlabeled or over-ceiling nodes.

The remainder of the upstream tree (CLI, admin UI, model SDKs, hosted
cache, markdown mutation) is not vendored.
